version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-22"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research repository for a doctoral study on Smart and Sustainable Cities
  investigating temporal and spatial relationships between urban sports and
  recreation infrastructure and premature mortality from non-communicable
  diseases among adults aged 30–69 years in São Paulo, Brazil. The project
  integrates GeoAI, GIS, artificial intelligence, spatial epidemiology, and
  data science to support evidence-based public policies.
keywords:
  - smart cities
  - sustainable cities
  - GeoAI
  - GIS
  - spatial epidemiology
  - non-communicable diseases
  - sports infrastructure
  - São Paulo
  - public policy
